BTW - When I talk about self-transformation, I'm speaking of mental, as
much as physical transformations.

Some points:

A) People change, whether or not you want them to. Trying to keep people
from changing will just stifle them.

B) My point was not just acceptance, but support. Of course, this is again
modified by personal taste. I'm far more supportive of changes I approve of
than the ones I don't. (See point C) This is something you can contribute
to the relationship. Remember, if your partners aren't receiving good value
for their time, they're going to shop elsewhere (to drop back to my "Love
is a Market" analogy).

