your partners, they will find it easier to make massive improvements in
thier life. I am currently helping Romana self-transform into a "media
icon", via Stego and her upcoming articles in WIRED and bOING bOING (maybe
even Future Sex). She does 90%, but my ten percent helps keep up her energy
and make such efforts easier for her. (Tim, you actually helped as well.
Providing the inspiration for the program, etc. Your contributions are not
unaknowledged or unappreciated.) By working on projects with her, I can use
this to further my own career. (Not that this is my only reason mind you.)

E) Ultimatums ("If you pierce your nipple, I don't ever want to see you
again!") have the unique quality of pissing people off, and often
encourages people to go ahead and do whatever it is that the giver of the
ultimatum was trying to prevent. (It has that effect on me. It's something
I've learned to watch for, since I'd prefer to make up my own mind.) They
also intimate (rightly or wrongly) a low value on the relationship.

Granted, people do sometimes grow apart, but I contend that supporting
self-transformations will actually decrease the risk.

